    <string name="tutorial_1_title">Budget your spending money</string>
    <string name="tutorial_1_body">Start outside the app. Take what you earn, subtract the bills that never change — rent, insurance, subscriptions, loan payments — and whatever is left is your spending money.\n\nSplit that across the weeks in the month, and you have your weekly target.</string>

    <string name="tutorial_2_title">Bills don\'t belong in here</string>
    <string name="tutorial_2_body">There is deliberately nowhere to enter recurring income or expenses. Those amounts are already fixed, so leaving them out keeps the app focused on the one number that actually moves: what you spent this week.\n\nIf money comes in mid-week — a refund, a gift, cash back — add it as an expense with a minus sign.</string>

    <string name="tutorial_3_title">Share it with your partner</string>
    <string name="tutorial_3_body">One budget can live on as many devices as you like, and they all stay in step.\n\nOpen Edit budget, tap Invite someone, and send the link. Whoever opens it joins this budget, and you will both see the same running total.\n\nThe link works once and expires after a week, so a forwarded one is harmless.</string>

    <string name="tutorial_4_title">On iPhone? There is an app</string>
    <string name="tutorial_4_body">There is an iPhone app too — listed as Weekly Spend, because this name was taken — and budget.andrewovens.com opens in any browser. All three work on the same budget.\n\nEdit budget has the links, under Apps for other devices.</string>

